[2026-01-30T13:03:46.557Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KNh3D8jvFq4j1H43aD8UtK","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n     2→\n     3→## REQUIREMENT\n     4→\n     5→# Debounce search input in FindingsTab and SourcesTab\n     6→\n     7→## Metadata\n     8→- **Category**: performance\n     9→- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    10→- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    11→- **Scan Type**: perf_optimizer\n    12→- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:35:45 AM\n    13→\n    14→## Description\n    15→Both FindingsTab and SourcesTab filter on every keystroke via onChange triggering setSearchQuery. Add 150-200ms debounce to the search input to batch keystrokes and reduce filter recalculations during rapid typing.\n    16→\n    17→## Reasoning\n    18→Users typing a search query trigger filter recalculation on every character. With 50+ items, this creates noticeable lag. Debouncing reduces recalculations by 80-90% and makes typing feel instant.\n    19→\n    20→## Context\n    21→\n    22→**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n    23→\n    24→### Context: Report Tabs\n    25→\n    26→**Description**: Tab-based navigation components for quick-access report sections. Provides compact, scannable summaries for overview, findings, sources, entities, analysis, and perspectives.\n    27→**Related Files**:\n    28→- `src/components/report/tabs/OverviewTab.tsx`\n    29→- `src/components/report/tabs/FindingsTab.tsx`\n    30→- `src/components/report/tabs/SourcesTab.tsx`\n    31→- `src/components/report/tabs/EntitiesTab.tsx`\n    32→- `src/components/report/tabs/AnalysisTab.tsx`\n    33→- `src/components/report/tabs/PerspectivesTab.tsx`\n    34→- `src/components/report/tabs/index.tsx`\n    35→\n    36→**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n    37→\n    38→## Recommended Skills\n    39→\n    40→Use Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills/` directory for available skills.\n    41→\n    42→## Notes\n    43→\n    44→This requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n    45→\n    46→## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n    47→\n    48→1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n    49→   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n    50→   - title: 2-6 word summary\n    51→   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n    52→\n    53→2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n    54→   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n    55→   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n    56→\n    57→3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n    58→\n    59→Begin implementation now.\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cec20cb-b613-4ab4-b437-0d4075a2df3d","uuid":"1f8fab68-794a-4f02-86e9-242a98860cec","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\idea-bcaa47ed-debounce-search-input-in-findi.md","content":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Debounce search input in FindingsTab and SourcesTab\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: performance\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: perf_optimizer\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:35:45 AM\n\n## Description\nBoth FindingsTab and SourcesTab filter on every keystroke via onChange triggering setSearchQuery. Add 150-200ms debounce to the search input to batch keystrokes and reduce filter recalculations during rapid typing.\n\n## Reasoning\nUsers typing a search query trigger filter recalculation on every character. With 50+ items, this creates noticeable lag. Debouncing reduces recalculations by 80-90% and makes typing feel instant.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Tabs\n\n**Description**: Tab-based navigation components for quick-access report sections. Provides compact, scannable summaries for overview, findings, sources, entities, analysis, and perspectives.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/tabs/OverviewTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/FindingsTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/SourcesTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/EntitiesTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/AnalysisTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/PerspectivesTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/index.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\nUse Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills/` directory for available skills.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n\n3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now.","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
